{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155725-rank-5-relic-idea-i-need-help-fleshing-it-out","id":155725,"title":"Rank 5 Relic Idea, I need help fleshing it out.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-01T10:07:39-07:00","id":155725,"title":"Rank 5 Relic Idea, I need help fleshing it out.","content":"I wanted to make a scion who had been obsessed with star wars as a kid and when he got his visitation started growing his powers and abilities to mimick a Jedi. It will be fun to make pop culture references and also very quickly become better than any Jedi could have been. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But how would you build a relic that works like a lightsaber? I was thinking something tied to the sun purview, but I have allocated a 5 dot relic for the thing.<br /> Does anyone have any ideas how to make it work? Have already done it and can link me the breakdown? Do you think this is a terrible idea and I should stick to normal material swords you crazy star wars nerd you? Please, by all means let me know.<br /> <br /> I was personally thinking Using the stats for a Spatha, but 1 dot of the power to only letting someone with the sun purview 'ignite' the blade, so it looks like a mag light or a movie prop to anyone else. Then one dot for sun purview access and the other 3 dots to make the blade cut through things like a Lightsaber would, but I don't know how to represent that mechanically. Piercing tag? Better than Piercing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T11:38:20-07:00","id":155785,"title":"","content":"Looking like a lightsaber should not cost you anything. You could do the same thing with a real sword that had a flashlight taped to it, or a glowing stick swung with titanium tools.<br /> <br /> Doing the things a lightsaber does is going to be a lot more expensive. I would recommend picking up holy rampage(one dot) and divine rampage(one dot), and then reducing the cost of divine rampage to free(one dot). You can have the weapon completely ignore armor (two dots) which would also simulate the ease of chopping things. If you already have those knacks then it is a little cheaper and you can buy legend to damage (two dots).<br /> <br /> If you have a conservative storyteller then all those prices might increase a dot, in which case definitely buy holy rampage and divine rampage the normal way. Then expect your whole relic to be free divine rampage (two dots) and completely ignore armor (three dots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T09:10:30-07:00","id":156581,"title":"","content":"I would also add in something like Whirlwind Shield so you can deflect ranged attacks with a stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}